# Failures Log — {{ preset }} preset

> Repeated mistakes / pitfalls in this project. The wrapup stage appends entries automatically.
>
> **Search:** `rg -F "[fail:" .claude/memory/failures.md`
>
> **Format:**
> ```
> ## [fail:<category>] <slug> | <YYYY-MM-DD> | count:<N>
> <reproduction trigger + root cause + resolution in one paragraph>
> - [<YYYY-MM-DD>] <one-line note for the 2nd occurrence>
> - [<YYYY-MM-DD>] <one-line note for the 3rd occurrence>
> ```
> - `category`: import / test / render / hook / lint / type / runtime / design / other
> - `count`: bump the heading only on repeats — same slug → count++ (never duplicate sections). wrapup searches existing slugs first and reuses the matching one, so recurrences accumulate instead of fragmenting.
> - Each repeat appends one dated occurrence bullet under the original body (first-seen date is kept in the heading), so a `count:N` entry carries N−1 occurrence lines of evidence.
> - When count ≥ 3, wrapup adds an improvement proposal to `.claude/memory/pending-proposals.md`

